# A retail broadband provider selling full fibre over two wholesale networks,
# Openreach and CityFibre: availability on both, a quote with speed tiers
# and extras such as digital voice, new lines and transfers (One Touch
# Switch), the wholesale order, building the service in its own systems,
# activation and aftercare. The provider is fictional.
# covers: §4.1, §4.2, §4.4, §4.6, §4.7, §6.4, §7.2, §7.4, §8, §9, §9.1, §10
title "Full-fibre broadband provisioning"
doc From a customer's quote request to a working, billed full-fibre line on Openreach or CityFibre, and the first check-in afterwards.

store Address database
store Product catalogue
store OSS inventory
store Billing system

pool Customer
  doc A household getting full-fibre broadband, new or switching from another provider.
  group Quote and order
    start Wants faster broadband
    send Request a quote ~> Quote requested
    event Wait for the quote
      - receive Offer received
        user Choose speed and extras
        doc For example 500 Mbps with digital voice, keeping the current phone number.
        send Place order ~> Customer order received
        event Wait for the provider
          - receive Order confirmed
          - receive Order declined -> end Order not accepted
      - receive No service at the address -> end Not available
  group Build
    receive Installation date
    receive Router arrives
  group Go live
    receive Installation done
    receive Welcome pack
    end Online

pool Courier [collapsed]
Courier ~> Router arrives
Courier ~> Delivery confirmed

pool CityFibre
  doc An alternative wholesale full-fibre network in many towns and cities.
  group Quote and order
    start message CityFibre availability request
    service Check CityFibre coverage
    send Return CityFibre availability ~> CityFibre availability
    end CityFibre answered
  group Build
    start message CityFibre order received
    service Validate CityFibre order
    xor CityFibre order valid?
      no:
        send Reject CityFibre order ~> Order rejected
        end CityFibre rejected
      yes:
        user Book installer
        send Commit CityFibre date ~> Committed date received
  group Go live
    user Install CityFibre connection
    send Send CityFibre completion ~> Completion notice
    end CityFibre order complete

pool Brightwave Broadband
  doc The retail provider: sells the service, builds it in its own systems and bills for it.
  lanes Sales [color: #E3F2FD], Credit and fraud [color: #E3F2FD]
  lanes Order management [color: #FFF8E1], Network provisioning [color: #E8F5E9]
  lanes Voice [color: #E8F5E9], Logistics [color: #E8F5E9]
  lanes Billing [color: #F3E5F5], Customer care [color: #F3E5F5]

  group Quote and order
    lane Sales
    start message Quote requested
    doc Quote requests arrive from the website with the address and, for a transfer, the current provider.
    service Find address key [reads: Address database]
    doc Looks up the UPRN and each network's address key for it.
    and Check both networks
      -
        send Ask Openreach for availability ~> Openreach availability request
        receive Openreach availability
      -
        send Ask CityFibre for availability ~> CityFibre availability request
        receive CityFibre availability
    xor Any full fibre available?
      yes:
        service Build offer [reads: Product catalogue]
        doc Speed tiers per available network (for example 150, 500 and 900 Mbps, and 2 Gbps on CityFibre), with extras: digital voice, number porting, a mesh Wi-Fi booster.
        send Send offer ~> Offer received
        receive Customer order received
        xor New line or transfer?
          new line:
            -> Run credit check
          transfer:
            service Request switch match ~(name, address, current provider)~> One Touch Switch hub
            receive Switch match received
            doc The hub returns a switch order reference and tells the current provider; their service ends on the switch date.
            -> Run credit check
      no:
        send Tell customer no service ~> No service at the address
        end No service

    lane Credit and fraud
    service Run credit check ~(applicant details)~> Credit agency
    receive Credit result
    xor Credit decision?
      pass:
        -> Confirm order
      refer:
        user Review application manually
        doc Fraud analysts check identity documents within one working day.
        xor Approved on review?
          yes:
            -> Confirm order
          no:
            -> Decline order
      fail:
        -> Decline order
    send Decline order ~> Order declined
    end Declined
    lane Sales
    send Confirm order ~> Order confirmed
    note Confirmation includes the earliest installation window

  group Build
    lane Order management
    service Place wholesale order [writes: Wholesale order]
    doc A new-provide or a transfer order, with the address key, the speed tier and the appointment preference.
    xor Which network?
      openreach:
        send Order from Openreach ~> Openreach order received
      cityfibre:
        send Order from CityFibre ~> CityFibre order received
    event Wait for the network
      - receive Committed date received
      - receive Order rejected
        user Correct order details
        doc Typical rejections: wrong address key, a tier the line cannot carry, missing access details.
        -> Place wholesale order
      - wait 2 working days
        user Chase the network
        -> Wait for the network
    send Tell customer the date ~> Installation date
    fork
      -
        lane Network provisioning
        service Reserve IP and service ID [writes: OSS inventory]
        service Configure RADIUS and speed profile
      -
        lane Voice
        xor Digital voice ordered?
          yes:
            service Set up digital voice line
            xor Keep current number?
              yes: service Port phone number ~> One Touch Switch hub
              no: service Allocate new number
          no:
      -
        lane Logistics
        service Dispatch router ~(shipping order)~> Courier
        receive Delivery confirmed
      -
        lane Billing
        service Create billing account [writes: Billing system]
        doc The account is created now but stays inactive until the line is live.

  group Go live
    lane Order management
    receive Completion notice
    send Confirm installation ~> Installation done
    lane Network provisioning
    sub Activate service
      start
      service Bind service ID to the ONT
      service Push configuration
      service Run line tests
      xor Tests pass?
        yes: end Service active
        no: end error Activation failed
      on error Activation failed
        lane Customer care
        user Troubleshoot with the customer
        doc Remote checks first; a second network visit is booked only if the fault is on the network side.
        -> Activate service
    lane Billing
    service Start billing [writes: Billing system]
    lane Customer care
    send Send welcome pack ~> Welcome pack
    end Customer live

  group Aftercare
    lane Customer care
    start timer 14 days after go-live
    user Satisfaction call
    xor Customer happy?
      yes: end Case closed
      no:
        user Raise service ticket
        end Ticket raised

pool Openreach
  doc The national wholesale network that builds and connects the fibre.
  lanes Order handling [color: #FFF3E0], Planning [color: #FFF3E0], Field engineering [color: #FFE0B2]

  group Quote and order
    lane Order handling
    start message Openreach availability request
    service Check Openreach line plant
    send Return Openreach availability ~> Openreach availability
    end Openreach answered

  group Build
    lane Order handling
    start message Openreach order received
    service Validate Openreach order
    xor Openreach order valid?
      no:
        send Reject Openreach order ~> Order rejected
        end Openreach rejected
      yes:
        xor Order type?
          new provide:
            lane Planning
            sub Survey and plan route [collapsed]
            doc Desk survey of ducts and poles; a site survey when the route is unclear.
            user Book engineer appointment
            send Commit Openreach date ~> Committed date received
            lane Field engineering
            user Install fibre and ONT [stroke: #E65100]
              on timer Appointment missed [non-interrupting] -> send Notify delay ~> Brightwave Broadband -> end Delay notified
          transfer:
            service Schedule remote switch-over
            doc The existing fibre and ONT stay; the line moves to the new provider on the switch date.
            send Commit switch date ~> Committed date received
            service Switch over remotely

  group Go live
    lane Order handling
    service Close Openreach work order
    send Send Openreach completion ~> Completion notice
    end Openreach order complete

pool Credit agency [collapsed]
Credit agency ~> Credit result

pool One Touch Switch hub [collapsed]
One Touch Switch hub ~> Switch match received
